    "summary": "approval-gate.ts is generalized: authorizeStageChange maps an artifact to its stage unit(s) and asks a decide function; authorizeApproval (approve-local) is unchanged in behaviour, authorizeFindingApply asks review-fix, and reviewFixModeFor decides through reviewFixDecision (apply-auto-fixes only when every unit allows). resolveReviewFinding (resolve.ts) calls authorizeFindingApply for action apply before reading the markdown or writing anything and throws TeamGateRefusedError for a non-holder; accept, override and defer are untouched. Both automatic review paths consult reviewFixModeFor before applyAutoFixes (verdicts.ts and run-artifact.ts) and, when report-only, skip the fixes so the review still runs, stamps its findings, writes meta only and keeps the revision. The terminal resolve case prints '✗ not applied — <reason>'. Tests: gate-resolve-finding.test.ts (apply refused with markdown and artifact byte-identical, accept/override/defer still run, holder and no-policy apply work), gate-review-fix.test.ts (verdicts phase and reviewArtifactFile: non-holder reports findings, applies no fix and keeps revision 2; holder applies and mints revision 3), and a resolve test in gate-refusal-output.test.ts. The review, cli, workflow and review-step suites pass apart from the known TUI poll-interval timing flake.",
